      "id": "ctkg:statement-argument:f80186ee6c03d998fdc49342",
      "canonicalType": "StatementArgument",
      "label": "1) A necessary and sufficient condition for every equilibrium state of the system to be stable in the sense of Lyapunov is that all eigenvalues of A have non-positive (negative or zero) real parts, and any eigenvalue with zero real part is a simple root of the minimal polynomial of A. 2) A necessary and sufficient condition for the unique equilibrium state xₑ=0 of the system to be asymptotically stable is that all eigenvalues of A have negative real parts.",
